(7356139, 1151045, 16106, '<td valign="top">Part of the power of the original was that razor sharpness of the narrow depth of field and all the blur of the rest. While much of this image is a fine interpretation, the areas in focus and those that are blurred just don''t make sense to me. The hand below the subject''s face looks like it ought to be in the same plane as her eyes but they are vague and lacking in detail. I like what is here, but I miss the little details that ought to be in the frame.</td>', 'Part of the power of the original was that razor sharpness of the narrow depth of field and all the blur of the rest. While much of this image is a fine interpretation, the areas in focus and those that are blurred just don''t make sense to me. The hand below the subject''s face looks like it ought to be in the same plane as her eyes but they are vague and lacking in detail. I like what is here, but I miss the little details that ought to be in the frame.', '2015-06-01 16:50:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(7356140, 1150939, 68504, '<td valign="top">very close, but totally lacking in the character contributed by the original models'' maturity and expression.</td>', 'very close, but totally lacking in the character contributed by the original models'' maturity and expression.', '2015-06-01 16:52:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(7356142, 1150749, 16106, '<td valign="top">Oliver is perhaps the best guy with studio light on the site, so taking on one of his images is always a challenge, and for a shot like this the details are key. His light on the left with a touch of bounce to fill in the right side with the darkest part being closest to the camera made his shot spectacular. Here the even left right light, and the touch too much empty frame along the bottom come up a bit short. Still you got 90% of it, just not the touch of magic.</td>', 'Oliver is perhaps the best guy with studio light on the site, so taking on one of his images is always a challenge, and for a shot like this the details are key. His light on the left with a touch of bounce to fill in the right side with the darkest part being closest to the camera made his shot spectacular. Here the even left right light, and the touch too much empty frame along the bottom come up a bit short. Still you got 90% of it, just not the touch of magic.', '2015-06-01 16:57:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(7356143, 1150964, 68504, '<td valign="top">boobles.</td>', 'boobles.', '2015-06-01 16:57:27.000000', NULL, 1),
